.TH tukanban n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tukanban
.PP
Parses a Mermaid \fBkanban\fR block and renders it natively (SVG or PNG) through the pure\-Tcl engine. A self\-contained 2D renderer in the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR family (like \fBtupie\fR / \fBtusankey\fR / \fBtupacket\fR); normally you call \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR / \fBtuflow::toPng\fR, which dispatch here. A kanban board is a column layout, not a node\-edge graph, so it does \fBnot\fR go through \fBtudiagram\fR.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tukanban 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tukanban::parse text                          ;# -> kanban model dict
::tclutils::tukanban::toSvg  model ?-width W? ?-height H? ?-fontfile f? ?-scale n?
::tclutils::tukanban::toPng  model ?...?                  ;# -> PNG bytes
::tclutils::tukanban::writeSvg model file ?...?
::tclutils::tukanban::writePng model file ?...?
.CE
.SS "Supported syntax (Mermaid subset)"
.CS
kanban
  <Column Title>                 -> least-indented content line
    <Card text>                  -> a more-indented line
    <Card text>@{ key: val, ... } -> optional metadata
.CE
.IP \(bu
The header line is \fBkanban\fR; columns and cards follow.
.IP \(bu
\fBIndentation decides the role.\fR The first content line after the header sets the column indent; lines at that indent are column titles, deeper lines are cards of the current column.
.IP \(bu
Card metadata after \fB@{ ... }\fR: a \fBpriority\fR value is pulled out and shown as a colour badge in the card's top\-right (High = red, Medium = orange, Low = green, Critical/Blocked = dark red, anything else = grey). The remaining \fBkey: value\fR pairs are shown as a small grey sub\-line. The Mermaid keys \fBticket\fR, \fBassigned\fR, \fBpriority\fR are typical but not required.
.IP \(bu
Blank lines and \fB%%\fR comments are ignored.
.SS "Layout (v1)"
.PP
Columns are laid out left\-to\-right and fill the canvas evenly. Each column has a coloured header band (from a fixed qualitative palette), a light lane background, and its cards stacked top\-to\-bottom as rounded white boxes. A card with metadata is drawn taller to fit its sub\-line. The canvas size grows automatically with the column count and the tallest card stack when \fB\-width\fR / \fB\-height\fR are left at their default (\fB0\fR = auto).
.SS "v1 limitations (honest)"
.IP \(bu
\fBpriority\fR is styled as a badge; other metadata is one joined grey line.
.IP \(bu
No card background colours or assignee avatars; long text is clipped.
.IP \(bu
Long card text is clipped to the column width, not wrapped or shrunk.
.IP \(bu
Cards exceeding the lane height are dropped (the lane does not scroll).
.SS Options
.PP
\fB\-width\fR (default \fB0\fR = auto from column count), \fB\-height\fR (default \fB0\fR = auto from the tallest stack), \fB\-fontfile\fR (a TTF for real\-font labels via \fBGlyphs\fR; PNG only \-\- otherwise the built\-in 6x8 bitmap font with German umlauts via real codepoints), \fB\-scale\fR (positive integer; enlarges the PNG canvas, SVG ignores it).
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tukanban
set src {kanban
    Backlog
        Write the spec
        Design the API@{ ticket: DOC-1, priority: High }
    In Progress
        Implement parser@{ assigned: Dev }
    Done
        Review complete@{ ticket: DOC-99 }}
::tclutils::tukanban::writePng [::tclutils::tukanban::parse $src] board.png -scale 3
.CE
.PP
In Markdown, \fBkanban\fR rides on the \fB```mermaid\fR fence, so docir's raster sinks (pdf / odt / rendererTk) render it through \fBtuflow::toPng\fR; no docir change is needed.
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Companion: \fBtclutils::tusvg\fR / \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR (canvas), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (dispatch).
.IP \(bu
Headers, lanes, cards and text use only rect/text primitives, so SVG and PNG stay congruent.
.IP \(bu
\fBtuflow::parse\fR rejects \fBkanban\fR with \fB{TCLUTILS TUFLOW UNSUPPORTED}\fR (it is not a node\-edge graph); the facade \fBtoSvg\fR/\fBtoPng\fR is the render path, exactly as for \fBpie\fR / \fBsankey\-beta\fR / \fBpacket\-beta\fR.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUKANBAN <REASON>}\fR \-\- \fBEMPTY\fR (no header / no columns), \fBARG\fR (bad \fB\-scale\fR), \fBFONT\fR (font file not found).
